    <main class="main-column">
      <VerificationBadge verifiedDate="26 October 2026" topic="2026/27 World Championship Qualification" />

      <section class="content-card">

<p>Staged in Alexandra Palace’s historic <strong>Great Hall</strong>, the expanded 128-player championship brings together the world's elite tour professionals, seasonal form leaders, secondary tour frontrunners, and champions from international partner circuits.</p>
<p>The 128 places are determined through three primary pathways:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>The PDC Order of Merit (40 players):</strong> The official world rankings based on two-year rolling prize money.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>The PDC ProTour Order of Merit (40 players):</strong> The highest-earning non-qualified players over a single season on the European Tour and Players Championship floor circuit.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>The International &amp; Secondary Tour Tier (48 places):</strong> An itemized ledger of developmental tours, women's pathways, continental affiliate champions, and the final Tour Card holder qualifier.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>Below is the verified breakdown of how all 128 spots are allocated under official Professional Darts Corporation (<a href="https://www.pdc.tv/">PDC</a>) and Professional Darts Players Association (<a href="https://pdpa.co.uk/">PDPA</a>) regulations.</p>
